# JES buttons and sliders
@scenario tutorial_lesson_39
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/39_jes_widgets.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt push_widgets]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Drag the slider and hover over Return in this JES scene. Click the button or press Esc to return.
@label lab
> Run the control panel -> widgets
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
@label widgets
# region push_widgets
[jes push scripts/scenes/widgets.jes label compare]
# endregion
@label compare
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/widgets.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt slider]
ginger: Change the slider default from 25 to 50 in widgets.jes and reopen it. The button's appearance and its return action can be edited independently.
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_39]
[flag tutorial_done_39]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_8]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Set value to 50 with the same min and max. What should you see?
> The slider range doubles. -> practice_hint
> The knob starts at the midpoint. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The initial value changes the starting knob position. The range is still 0 to 100.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: The initial value changes the starting knob position. The range is still 0 to 100.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the interactive lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Which component sets the current slider value?
> Slider2D. -> correct
> Label2D. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The slider defines min, max and value. Labels present text.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The slider defines min, max and value. Labels present text.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
